SWEET nav14 (patch 0258, T-18b3, G-10b-nav; input injection + one counter, no register, no store to hardware): (1) the About tap is gated on the General page: it waits until >= 55 swaps have been presented since the General tap and the swap counter has been flat >= 500 ms (polled every 100 ms, cap 4 s; the wait is before the `ACTION about-open begin` marker). Logs `SWEET NAV: about-open gate: S swaps since the General tap, counter flat F ms, waited W ms, satisfied|CAP` and, at the cap, `SWEET GAP: NAV about-open: general page not populated after 4 s ...`. (2) The about-open verify of patch 0256/0257 counts distinct frames (new global sweet_fb_distinct_count, incremented where the SWEET FPS `distinct` hash differs; needs boot-arg sweetfps, `SWEET GAP` and a swap-count fallback otherwise) instead of raw swaps; threshold unchanged at 20; retry/result lines now print `D distinct (S swaps)`. Reason [obs nav11-13, docs/reviews/T-c198-proof.md s2-s4]: the General push presents either one burst of 32-33 swaps (5 of 9 reps; the following About tap is lost) or 61-66 swaps (the tap lands), and nav13 rep 2 passed the 20-swap verify on a 20 Hz spinner (distinct 0). Whether the gate fixes the lost tap is the ticket's test; if About stays dead with the gate satisfied the model is wrong.
